        "original_id": "5856d73d-a1a7-5b63-862b-a12f44d25532",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richie Ginther, Bruce McLaren, Graham Hill\n- Events: 1962 Italian Grand Prix, 1963 Lombank Trophy, 2009 Monaco Grand Prix\n- Teams/Constructors: Cooper, BRM\n- Products/Cars: BRM P57\n- Places: Circuit de Monaco, Monaco\n\nFacts:\n- At the 1962 Italian Grand Prix, Richie Ginther finished second.\n- At the 1962 Italian Grand Prix, Cooper driver Bruce McLaren finished third.\n- Norman Graham Hill was born on 15 February 1929 and died on 29 November 1975.\n- Graham Hill was a British racing driver and team owner from England who won the Formula One World Championship twice.\n- The 1963 Lombank Trophy was run over 50 laps and was won by British driver Graham Hill in a BRM P57.\n- The 2009 Monaco Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 24 May 2009 at the Circuit de Monaco in Monaco.",
